/*
:name: undefined_generic_default
:type: error
:error: unknown type or lambda 'ZZ' in a generic default
:help: declare `ZZ` before its use
*/

// Ruling 2026-09-28 #24 (clarification): reading a name with no accessible
// declaration is a direct compile error at the read, in every context. A
// generic default is kept as source text that the runner re-reads at each
// call; before, an undeclared name there became nil and surfaced only as the
// indirect upass.tolg "unresolved reference 'inl1_ZZ' ... resolved to nil".
// User ruling 2026-09-28 (33): the error names what a generic default reads (a
// type, lambda or comptime const declared earlier), not a variable.
comb addn<N=ZZ>(a:U8) -> (r:U8) {  // locate_error_here
  r = (a + N)#[0..<8]
}

pub comb undefined_generic_default(a:U8) -> (r:U8) {
  r = addn(a=a)
}
